1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,132
Sworn makes private Tempo Zone execution checkable.

2
00:00:03,182 --> 00:00:11,314
Since my last check-in, it went from a test batch to a live run on our own Zone:

3
00:00:11,364 --> 00:00:19,495
on Moderato, the portal settled three batches only after the proof passed, and our sequencer paid a withdrawal.

4
00:00:19,545 --> 00:00:24,950
A forged batch, signed by our own sequencer, was rejected on chain.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,044
What I learned: the proof is necessary, not sufficient; our sequencer still pays.

6
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:33,856
And the hard part isn't proving.

7
00:00:33,906 --> 00:00:39,950
It's whether a Zone business's reviewer will pay for evidence it can check.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,421
Next: one design partner supplies a batch, and its reviewer decides.

9
00:00:46,471 --> 00:00:49,950
Everything is re-runnable from the repo.
